  "id": 35,
  "Specification": "CheckpointCoordination: A fault-tolerant distributed checkpoint coordination protocol over a set of nodes with a majority quorum. Models node/network failures and recoveries, Paxos-style leader election, replicated log propagation, and checkpoint lifecycle (start/finish). A lease mechanism controls which node may take a checkpoint at any time. Temporal invariants ensure checkpoints are eventually taken and liveness is maintained under fairness assumptions.",
